    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d602">

                <pb facs="0567" n="559" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg559"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94112/409: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-12-17T23:00:00+09:00">December 17, 1940—11
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 18—10:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1331. Shanghai’s 1394, December 14, 2 p.m.<anchor n="54" xml:id="d602-f1"/> In an
                    interview with the Foreign Minister today I brought orally to his attention the
                    further facts in connection with controversy of the American owned motor vessel
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Estelle L</hi> and stated that no progress had been
                    made toward obtaining the release of this vessel in negotiations with the
                    Japanese authorities in Shanghai. Our request under instructions for the release
                    of the vessel presented in a <hi rendition="#italic">note verbale</hi> of
                    December 10 was repeated.<anchor n="55" xml:id="d602-f2"/></p>
                <p>Sent to the Department via Shanghai.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d602-f1" n="54" xml:id="d602-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d602-f2" n="55" xml:id="d602-f2-content">
                <p>The <hi rendition="#italic">Estelle L</hi> was released on January 9, 1941.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
